1
00:00:38,761 --> 00:00:39,761
VALKYRIE - 2009

2
00:00:39,762 --> 00:00:43,262
<font size=17>sub. up. by :</font>
<font color="lime" size=17>npdv.indoheroes [at] yahoo.com</font>

3
00:00:55,439 --> 00:00:58,865
I swear by God this sacred oath:

4
00:00:59,928 --> 00:01:04,417
That I shall render unconditional
obedience to Adolf Hitler,

5
00:01:04,771 --> 00:01:07,449
Führer of the German Empire
and its people,

6
00:01:07,724 --> 00:01:10,245
Supreme Commander of the armed forces.

7
00:01:10,481 --> 00:01:13,237
And that I shall at all time
be ready, as a brave soldier,

8
00:01:13,513 --> 00:01:18,199
My life for this oath.

9
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:50,432
The promises of the Führer about
peace and prosperity have been destroyed

10
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:55,432
and left nothing but destruction.

11
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:03,432
The atrocities committed by Hitlers SS
are a disgrace for the honour of the German army.

12
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:10,232
In the officers corps
there is widespread disgust

13
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:14,536
about the crimes committed by the Nazis.

14
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:18,632
The killing of civilians,

15
00:02:18,798 --> 00:02:22,618
The torture and starving
of prisoners.

16
00:02:23,523 --> 00:02:26,319
The mass execution of Jews.

17
00:02:27,304 --> 00:02:31,084
My duty as an officer,
is no longer to save my country,

18
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:33,682
but to save human lives.

19
00:02:35,651 --> 00:02:40,022
I can not find one general, in a position
to confront Hitler,with the courage to do it.

20
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:44,078
Colonel Stauffenberg, sir.
The General'll be here in four hours.

21
00:02:44,629 --> 00:02:47,740
Thank you. I need to see him when he arrives.

22
00:02:51,362 --> 00:02:55,142
I found myself surrounded by men unwilling
or unable to face the truth.

23
00:02:56,127 --> 00:02:58,923
Hiltler is not only the arch-enemy
of the entire world,

24
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:01,876
but the arch-enemy of Germany.

25
00:03:03,805 --> 00:03:06,680
Change must be made.

26
00:03:13,728 --> 00:03:16,169
The British are moving up from the south,
Patton is closing in on the coast,

27
00:03:16,406 --> 00:03:20,461
You know we should have left two days ago.
- No, Colonel, we keep fighting.

28
00:03:21,013 --> 00:03:22,391
Until the final victory.

29
00:03:22,588 --> 00:03:26,092
North Africa is lost, and you're gonna need
these men a year from now to defend Berlin.

30
00:03:26,919 --> 00:03:30,581
We can serve Germany
or the Führer, not both.

31
00:03:32,589 --> 00:03:35,542
It's just that sort of talk
that had you sent here, Colonel.

32
00:03:35,779 --> 00:03:37,747
What I said was much worse.

33
00:03:39,519 --> 00:03:41,252
General.

34
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:45,977
I'm just trying to get
these men out of here alive.

35
00:03:53,892 --> 00:03:55,506
What would you have me do?

36
00:03:55,782 --> 00:04:00,389
You tell commander running low in water,
we have to re-route the 1st and the 21st panzer.

37
00:04:00,625 --> 00:04:03,263
At least then we'd have a chance.

38
00:04:03,499 --> 00:04:07,791
And records will show we didn't have
enough water to reach Sidi Mansour?

39
00:04:08,106 --> 00:04:09,996
I can guarantee it.

40
00:04:19,565 --> 00:04:21,022
See that it's done.

41
00:04:21,730 --> 00:04:23,463
General.

42
00:08:05,269 --> 00:08:06,568
Sit.

43
00:08:24,445 --> 00:08:27,674
Hitler's leaving.
- Yeah, the fuse.

44
00:08:59,765 --> 00:09:02,718
Colonel Brandt.

45
00:09:04,451 --> 00:09:06,577
Our regards to Colonel Stieff.

46
00:09:07,758 --> 00:09:13,192
Cointreau,
Let's hope I don't get
thirsty on the flight.

47
00:09:49,694 --> 00:09:51,151
He's landed.

48
00:09:58,829 --> 00:10:02,176
This is General Tresckow, connect me
with operations, Colonel Brandt.

49
00:10:04,972 --> 00:10:06,704
Colonel, Tresckow.

50
00:10:07,177 --> 00:10:08,870
I'm glad you arrived safely.

51
00:10:09,106 --> 00:10:11,666
I hate to trouble you but it seems
you have the wrong bottles for Colonel Stieff.

52
00:10:14,383 --> 00:10:16,273
You do still have the package?

53
00:10:19,777 --> 00:10:26,156
I've been called to Berlin unexpectedly, I can be at
your office first thing tomorrow morning to pick it up.

54
00:10:26,629 --> 00:10:29,700
Sorry for the inconvenience Colonel.
Yes, thank you.

55
00:10:32,417 --> 00:10:33,992
Do you think he knows?

56
00:10:35,528 --> 00:10:37,575
There is only one way,
to find out.

57
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,672
We've been discovered.
- What makes you think that?

58
00:10:51,908 --> 00:10:54,428
Oster's been arrested.
the Gestapo came for him last night.

59
00:10:54,704 --> 00:10:56,397
The Gestapo could have
arrested him for anything.

60
00:10:56,673 --> 00:10:59,390
What do you think went wrong?
- We don't know.

61
00:10:59,626 --> 00:11:04,115
The fuse, the temperature, the point is
the damned thing didn't go off.

62
00:11:14,274 --> 00:11:16,479
General Tresckow to see Colonel Brandt.

63
00:11:16,754 --> 00:11:18,487
The Colonel's expecting you, sir.

64
00:11:28,449 --> 00:11:30,024
At ease.

65
00:11:39,750 --> 00:11:44,042
You'll forgive me General, this little
round-up is having me writing reports all day.

66
00:11:44,672 --> 00:11:45,932
Round-up?

67
00:11:46,523 --> 00:11:50,421
Dissenters. Another plot against the Führer.

68
00:11:51,209 --> 00:11:53,020
Who are these people?

69
00:11:55,697 --> 00:11:57,509
You'd be surprised.

70
00:12:02,549 --> 00:12:05,896
Is this what you've come for?

71
00:12:12,708 --> 00:12:15,346
Perhaps we should open it.

72
00:12:16,370 --> 00:12:17,630
I beg your pardon?

73
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:22,552
Well, you've come a long way,
you must be thirsty.

74
00:12:27,489 --> 00:12:30,690
You know, I wonder how the
Führer, who does not partaked,

75
00:12:30,691 --> 00:12:33,892
would feel about a
soldier who did so on duty.

76
00:12:40,622 --> 00:12:42,752
Colonel Brandt.

77
00:12:44,248 --> 00:12:46,650
I took you for an unsort, General.

78
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:50,233
And I you

79
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:00,786
We're still in business.

80
00:13:01,534 --> 00:13:03,149
Find a replacement for Oster.

81
00:13:03,385 --> 00:13:05,236
There is no-one we can trust,
not in Berlin.

82
00:13:05,511 --> 00:13:07,953
Then stop looking in Berlin.

83
00:13:34,138 --> 00:13:35,516
Frau von Stauffenberg.

84
00:13:36,973 --> 00:13:39,887
Perhaps, before you go in, we could
have a word together in my office.

85
00:13:40,123 --> 00:13:42,052
I will see my husband now.

86
00:13:49,455 --> 00:13:52,054
The right hand has been amputated above the wrist.

87
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:55,046
He's missing the fourth and fifth fingers
on the left hand.

88
00:13:55,361 --> 00:13:58,000
We couldn't save the left eye.

89
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:56,040
Colonel.

90
00:14:57,891 --> 00:14:59,308
Are you ready, sir?

91
00:15:39,905 --> 00:15:42,819
I'm a soldier, I serve my country.

92
00:15:44,118 --> 00:15:46,323
But this is my country.

93
00:15:46,559 --> 00:15:49,198
I was lying out there,
bleeding to death, thinking

94
00:15:49,434 --> 00:15:53,371
if I die now,
I leave nothing to my children but shame.

95
00:15:56,325 --> 00:15:59,750
I know now there is only one way
to serve Germany.

96
00:16:01,286 --> 00:16:03,924
And doing so I'll be a traitor

97
00:16:04,279 --> 00:16:06,011
I accept that.

98
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:10,618
Just tell me,
Can these men see it through?

99
00:16:12,469 --> 00:16:16,131
We need to reorganize,
reconsider our strategy.

100
00:16:16,406 --> 00:16:18,100
Recruit new men.

101
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:21,092
That's why we want you.

102
00:16:22,707 --> 00:16:28,259
You understand what will happen to my wife
and children, if these men can't see it through?

103
00:16:31,645 --> 00:16:34,598
Come and hear what they have to say.

104
00:16:46,490 --> 00:16:48,537
You know where to find us.

105
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:19,487
Enough, enough. I am not gonna listen to another
word of this. You had your chance, you failed.

106
00:17:19,763 --> 00:17:23,425
Your so-called central solution didn't work.

107
00:17:23,779 --> 00:17:26,023
Our only option now is to confront Hitler openly

108
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:27,874
This is a military operation.

109
00:17:28,110 --> 00:17:30,315
It is not a military operation,
it is a political organization.

110
00:17:30,552 --> 00:17:32,914
And one that has given
it's military arm too much control.

111
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:35,513
In any military exercise you have to
expect a certain measure of deviation.

112
00:17:35,789 --> 00:17:39,136
A measure?
What about total, complete, utter failure?

113
00:17:39,372 --> 00:17:41,498
Gentlemen, i think it's time we faced the fact

114
00:17:41,774 --> 00:17:45,633
The allies are coming come sooner or later.

115
00:17:45,869 --> 00:17:47,326
I say we sit back
and let them wipe out the Nazis.

116
00:17:47,562 --> 00:17:50,200
And ask every living soul in Europe
to pay the price. Use your head.

117
00:17:50,437 --> 00:17:53,823
Carl, please.
- I'm sorry Ludwig, I've held my tongue too long.

118
00:17:54,059 --> 00:17:57,012
We must now confront Hitler now.
Force him out.

119
00:17:57,249 --> 00:17:58,509
And then what?

120
00:18:00,517 --> 00:18:01,816
I beg your pardon?

121
00:18:03,076 --> 00:18:04,848
When Hitler's gone, then what?

122
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,573
I'm sorry, who is this man?

123
00:18:09,731 --> 00:18:12,212
Colonel Stauffenberg is Oster's replacement.

124
00:18:12,448 --> 00:18:15,283
He's been transferred to my office,
at the War Ministry.

125
00:18:16,543 --> 00:18:20,166
How is your uncle?
- He is well sir, he sends his regards.

126
00:18:20,362 --> 00:18:23,316
He speaks very highly of you.
- And of you, General.

127
00:18:23,513 --> 00:18:28,238
One of the things that made Oster such a great organizer,
Was that he kept his opinions to himself.

128
00:18:30,010 --> 00:18:33,002
I am simply asking what you intend to do
when Hitler is gone.

129
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:36,625
You don't really believe you can just
walk into the Reich chancellary ...

130
00:18:36,861 --> 00:18:38,869
And command the army to end the war?

131
00:18:39,066 --> 00:18:40,759
Yes, we do.

132
00:18:46,351 --> 00:18:49,343
You are in the presence of men
who would have been Hitler's inner circle.

133
00:18:50,052 --> 00:18:52,415
Instead we refused, Colonel.

134
00:18:52,651 --> 00:18:55,604
The people know we put our principles
above personal gain.

135
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:58,006
We have the respect of the people

136
00:18:58,282 --> 00:18:59,660
And the army.

137
00:19:01,865 --> 00:19:03,440
Then you don't need me.

138
00:19:05,487 --> 00:19:07,220
Gentlemen.

139
00:19:09,819 --> 00:19:12,142
Those men are confusing respect with popularity

140
00:19:12,614 --> 00:19:16,670
The army swore an oath.
An oath that won't just die with Hitler.

141
00:19:16,906 --> 00:19:20,608
How are we gonna deal with Goebbels,
Himmler and the SS?

142
00:19:20,844 --> 00:19:22,774
They will wipe you out.
-It doesn't matter.

143
00:19:25,569 --> 00:19:29,704
It only matters that we act, now.
Before we lose the war.

144
00:19:30,452 --> 00:19:34,271
Otherwise, this will always be
Hitler's Germany.

145
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:40,375
And we have to show the world...
that not all of us were like him.

146
00:19:40,611 --> 00:19:42,580
That is not enough for me.

147
00:19:43,879 --> 00:19:46,557
There has to be a chance of success.

148
00:19:47,738 --> 00:19:49,589
Then find a way.

149
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:55,534
Papa is home.

150
00:20:08,804 --> 00:20:11,521
I thought we agreed I'd come see you in Bamberg.

151
00:20:11,797 --> 00:20:13,844
The children couldn't wait.

152
00:20:14,356 --> 00:20:16,128
The children?

153
00:22:38,945 --> 00:22:40,284
Valkyrie.

154
00:22:40,638 --> 00:22:42,332
We've already considered Valkyrie,
it isn't suitable.

155
00:22:42,607 --> 00:22:45,403
Not as it's currently written. But the Colonel
has an idea, i think we should consider.

156
00:22:45,639 --> 00:22:48,829
Excuse me, what is Valkyrie?
- Operation Valkyrie.

157
00:22:49,025 --> 00:22:51,782
The reserve army has thousands
of men all over Berlin.

158
00:22:51,979 --> 00:22:56,664
Valkyrie is Hitler's contingency plan, to mobilize
those men during a national emergency.

159
00:22:56,901 --> 00:23:00,484
The sole purpose of the order is to protect
Hitler's government if he's cut off or killed.

160
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,335
And what use is this to us?

161
00:23:02,571 --> 00:23:05,603
Valkyrie is designed to contain civil unrest.

162
00:23:06,115 --> 00:23:09,147
But what if the SS were staging a coup?

163
00:23:12,730 --> 00:23:16,746
State security is trying to overthrow Hitler,
how would high command respond?

164
00:23:16,943 --> 00:23:19,188
We would have no choice, we would declare
a military state of emergency.

165
00:23:19,463 --> 00:23:23,598
- Exactly, and initiate Valkyrie.
- Hitler's own reserve army using Hitler's own plan.

166
00:23:23,834 --> 00:23:26,354
We'll have no choice but to seize power in Berlin

167
00:23:26,551 --> 00:23:28,953
To prevent the SS take-over.

168
00:23:29,977 --> 00:23:33,087
They'll think they're fightin
for Hitler's government, not against it.

169
00:23:33,324 --> 00:23:36,474
While we quietly put a new government in place.

170
00:23:37,655 --> 00:23:39,348
But only if he's dead.

171
00:23:40,529 --> 00:23:41,829
That's what you're saying, isn't it?

172
00:23:42,065 --> 00:23:45,136
How else are you gonna convince people
the SS are trying to seize power?

173
00:23:45,766 --> 00:23:49,350
We have to kill Hitler.
- I'm disappointed in you, Colonel.

174
00:23:49,625 --> 00:23:53,130
I thought a man of your background,
would suggest a more honorable approach.

175
00:23:53,602 --> 00:23:56,831
Your plan has a few minor obstacles, Colonel.

176
00:23:57,264 --> 00:24:00,099
First,  Valkyrie would have to be re-written,
to exclude the SS.

177
00:24:00,336 --> 00:24:03,013
And I'll need your help to get a copy.

178
00:24:03,958 --> 00:24:05,848
Rewriting an order is one thing.

179
00:24:07,345 --> 00:24:09,431
Distributing it is another.

180
00:24:09,825 --> 00:24:14,393
In this case we'd be wilfully circulating
written evidence of high-treason.

181
00:24:14,629 --> 00:24:16,834
Evidence requiring Hitler's signature.

182
00:24:22,583 --> 00:24:24,749
Well, we can all draw straws for the job.

183
00:24:26,127 --> 00:24:28,489
And what about Fromm?
- Fromm, who is Fromm?

184
00:24:28,726 --> 00:24:30,025
He's the commander of the reserve army.

185
00:24:30,261 --> 00:24:34,042
I can put the reserve troops on alert,
but only Fromm can initiate Valkyrie.

186
00:24:37,585 --> 00:24:39,436
Can you get to him?

187
00:24:42,429 --> 00:24:45,146
We're running out of time,
can you get to Fromm?

188
00:24:45,461 --> 00:24:46,996
He's a carreerist pig.

189
00:24:47,233 --> 00:24:49,083
But one who's gone as far
as he could go in Hitler's army.

190
00:24:49,319 --> 00:24:51,367
It's no secret he's not happy about it.

191
00:24:51,643 --> 00:24:54,123
Offer him a key position in the new regime.

192
00:24:54,950 --> 00:24:56,880
Make him see the light.

193
00:25:10,425 --> 00:25:12,473
Colonel Stauffenberg,
for General Fromm.

194
00:25:13,063 --> 00:25:16,961
Colonel Stauffenberg, sir. Welcome back.
It's an honor, sir.

195
00:25:18,891 --> 00:25:23,577
I 'd send you to the front, but i think
you'd surrender just to be Montgomery's whore.

196
00:25:29,129 --> 00:25:30,940
The General will see you now.

197
00:25:44,997 --> 00:25:46,848
What is it you want?

198
00:25:47,478 --> 00:25:51,416
I wanted to introduce our new man,
Colonel Stauffenberg.

199
00:25:52,872 --> 00:25:54,684
Ah, from Africa.

200
00:25:55,432 --> 00:26:00,078
I'd offer you my hand,
but I might not get it back.

201
00:26:00,315 --> 00:26:03,661
I'd say the General has lost
more important things this morning.

202
00:26:10,670 --> 00:26:13,466
It's about time they put somebody
with balls into this office.

203
00:26:13,702 --> 00:26:17,601
Please sit down, Colonel.
And you, Olbricht, if you must.

204
00:26:29,374 --> 00:26:33,981
They tell me you're critical of the war, Colonel.
Not that you don't seem to have good reason.

205
00:26:33,981 --> 00:26:36,226
I am critical of indecision, General.

206
00:26:36,462 --> 00:26:38,116
In the field?
- In Berlin.

207
00:26:40,596 --> 00:26:43,195
So that's why you're here, i take it ...

208
00:26:43,431 --> 00:26:46,148
- To make decisions.
- I have already made my decision.

209
00:26:46,345 --> 00:26:48,826
I'm here to help others make theirs.

210
00:26:53,078 --> 00:26:58,512
They say when there's no clear option,
the best thing is to do nothing.

211
00:26:58,749 --> 00:27:01,781
We're at war, we must act.

212
00:27:01,977 --> 00:27:03,986
Sometimes rational.

213
00:27:05,521 --> 00:27:08,593
And what rash action
did you have in mind, Colonel?

214
00:27:10,207 --> 00:27:15,287
That would be a decision
for the supreme military commander, sir.

215
00:27:15,562 --> 00:27:18,397
The supreme commander?

216
00:27:20,642 --> 00:27:22,650
Second only to the Chancellor.

217
00:27:27,651 --> 00:27:29,935
If I were that man ...

218
00:27:31,549 --> 00:27:34,305
Tis war would be going quite differently.

219
00:27:35,172 --> 00:27:37,062
Well, we were thinking the same, really.

220
00:27:45,882 --> 00:27:56,316
I don't need to remind you
that we've all sworn an oath to the Führer.

221
00:28:04,034 --> 00:28:06,987
Having said that, I'm going to forget
this conversation ever took place.

222
00:28:07,224 --> 00:28:09,704
In the strict understanding that such talk

223
00:28:09,941 --> 00:28:12,579
never occurs again under this roof.
Is that clear?

224
00:28:12,815 --> 00:28:17,186
You can tell your friends, Colonel, that i
I always come down on the right side.

225
00:28:17,422 --> 00:28:22,620
And as long as the Führer is alive
you know what side that is.

226
00:29:29,520 --> 00:29:32,158
Do you realize how close i am to Hitler?

227
00:29:32,394 --> 00:29:35,072
With one word i can make you disappear.

228
00:29:36,253 --> 00:29:38,655
My associates don't know we've been talking,
if that's what you are afraid of.

229
00:29:38,931 --> 00:29:42,789
When the SS catch you
they will pull you apart like warm bread.

230
00:29:43,026 --> 00:29:45,625
It would be a crime just to have known you then.

231
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:50,507
I warn you, don't try to contact me again.

232
00:29:50,704 --> 00:29:56,414
You won't report me. Maybe if you had when I first
approached you, you might have been keeping your oath.

233
00:29:56,571 --> 00:30:00,666
Now you're just as guilty as the rest of us.
- And i guess that makes me a sympathizer?

234
00:30:00,902 --> 00:30:03,423
Give a man a choice to betray
his fellow officers or his Führer

235
00:30:03,659 --> 00:30:05,667
And you think his actions will show you his heart.

236
00:30:05,903 --> 00:30:08,581
- It is not that simple.
- Yes..yes it is.

237
00:30:08,856 --> 00:30:12,046
For the last time, don't push me to make a decision.

238
00:30:12,282 --> 00:30:14,172
I don't have a choice, it's clear now.

239
00:30:16,613 --> 00:30:19,409
Without you, there is no hope of success.

240
00:30:20,315 --> 00:30:22,520
You're nothing but rats,
jumping from a sinking ship.

241
00:30:22,796 --> 00:30:25,001
What makes you think you'll be any different?

242
00:30:25,276 --> 00:30:26,733
What makes you think
you're stronger than the people?

243
00:30:27,009 --> 00:30:31,813
The Reich, the very momentum of history?
- This is going to happen, action is inevitable

244
00:30:32,049 --> 00:30:33,506
As are the consequences.

245
00:30:33,781 --> 00:30:38,585
When they come for me I'll do everything I can
to hide what you are doing, but don't delude yourself

246
00:30:38,822 --> 00:30:42,641
You were involved in a crime against your country
long before you met me.

247
00:30:44,374 --> 00:30:47,091
And there may still be time to redeem yourself.

248
00:30:50,359 --> 00:30:52,839
Only God can judge us now.

249
00:30:59,297 --> 00:31:04,062
Hitler had operation Valkyrie designed
to completely secure his government in six hours.

250
00:31:04,298 --> 00:31:07,802
I'm rewriting the orders so we can
seize control of the government in three.

251
00:31:08,393 --> 00:31:12,331
As written the orders spreads reserve troops
across all of Germany's 19 military districts.

252
00:31:12,606 --> 00:31:16,859
Including occupied cities like Paris,
Vienna and Prague.

253
00:31:17,095 --> 00:31:19,655
This is a waste of resources
since all of these districts

254
00:31:19,891 --> 00:31:25,443
Follow orders from Berlin without question.
If you take Berlin you take Germany.

255
00:31:25,679 --> 00:31:31,467
I'm rewriting Valkyrie to direct the majority
of our strongest units to focus entirely on Berlin.

256
00:31:32,334 --> 00:31:35,169
We'll surround the government quarter, occupy all
S.S. and police barracks.

257
00:31:35,366 --> 00:31:39,776
Once we have control of the government
we'll shut down all concentration camps.

258
00:31:40,012 --> 00:31:42,493
Any officers who resist will be arrested.

259
00:31:42,768 --> 00:31:45,722
I've been transferred to the front.

260
00:31:48,163 --> 00:31:52,101
Anyway, it doesn't matter.
You know these orders better than anyone.

261
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:55,251
That's why I am putting you in charge
of the military wing of the operation.

262
00:31:55,566 --> 00:31:58,676
- Beck agrees.
- Why not Olbricht?

263
00:31:58,913 --> 00:32:01,984
No, it is your plan.
It's you.

264
00:32:02,220 --> 00:32:06,827
You need to be absolutely certain no conflicting
order get out after the flash.

265
00:32:07,063 --> 00:32:08,599
It is not enough to kill Hitler.

266
00:32:08,875 --> 00:32:13,403
You need to isolate his chain of command and
cut them off from the outside world immediately.

267
00:32:13,679 --> 00:32:15,529
I already considered that.

268
00:32:16,159 --> 00:32:19,191
- I think I have just the man who can help.
- Who is he?

269
00:32:20,333 --> 00:32:22,341
Perhaps it's better I don't say.

270
00:32:26,082 --> 00:32:28,957
God promised Abraham he would not destroy Sodom

271
00:32:29,193 --> 00:32:31,319
If he could find ten righteous men.

272
00:32:31,910 --> 00:32:36,162
I have a feeling that, for Germany,
it may come down to one.

273
00:32:41,833 --> 00:32:43,368
Let's begin.

274
00:32:43,998 --> 00:32:47,542
The Führer, Adolf Hitler,

275
00:32:49,826 --> 00:32:51,558
Is dead.

276
00:32:57,898 --> 00:32:59,434
Heil Hiltler, General.

277
00:33:02,308 --> 00:33:04,198
Would you excuse us?

278
00:33:12,428 --> 00:33:17,074
- You play the part of bureaucrat beautifully.
- I see  it's my turn to relax.

279
00:33:17,310 --> 00:33:20,854
You've been promoted chief of staff
for the reserve army.

280
00:33:21,917 --> 00:33:24,910
Excuse me?
- Congratulations.

281
00:33:26,052 --> 00:33:28,257
I am busy with other things.

282
00:33:28,493 --> 00:33:32,195
Unfortunately, your nocturnal activities
don't count as service to the 'Reich'.

283
00:33:32,588 --> 00:33:35,069
I'll refuse the promotion.
- You'll do no such thing.

284
00:33:35,581 --> 00:33:39,794
Tresckow may have left you in charge of the operation
but in this world I still outrank you.

285
00:33:40,070 --> 00:33:41,920
You will accept the promotion.

286
00:33:42,432 --> 00:33:46,252
You'll have real access to Hitler,
his advisers, his schedule.

287
00:33:46,449 --> 00:33:48,024
We need this.

288
00:33:49,678 --> 00:33:52,828
I've looked through your changes to Valkyrie.

289
00:33:53,733 --> 00:33:57,592
I approve.
I need you to get Hitler to sign it.

290
00:34:00,900 --> 00:34:03,971
Now, there's a man here
to interview as your adjudant.

291
00:34:04,207 --> 00:34:06,176
He comes highly recommended.

292
00:34:12,673 --> 00:34:14,288
Close the door.

293
00:34:18,265 --> 00:34:19,525
Be seated.

294
00:34:23,305 --> 00:34:26,100
Do you know how this world
will end, Lieutenant?

295
00:34:26,337 --> 00:34:32,007
The portrait will be unhung,
and that man will be hung.

296
00:34:39,370 --> 00:34:42,756
I'm engaged in high treason
with all means available to me.

297
00:34:43,032 --> 00:34:44,568
Can I count you in?

298
00:34:51,459 --> 00:34:54,609
For anything, sir.
Anything at all.

299
00:35:52,570 --> 00:35:54,067
Come.

300
00:36:01,469 --> 00:36:03,084
Colonel Brandt, operations.

301
00:36:03,359 --> 00:36:06,943
Colonel Stauffenberg, I'd like to review
your presentation to the Führer.

302
00:36:07,966 --> 00:36:09,463
Strictly routine.

303
00:36:09,738 --> 00:36:11,904
Sir, the contents of the Colonel's
bag are for the Führer eyes only.

304
00:36:12,140 --> 00:36:13,991
I am the Führer's eyes, Lieutenant.

305
00:36:14,227 --> 00:36:17,928
The Colonel is a member of my staff at
the War Ministry. He doesn't answer to you.

306
00:36:19,858 --> 00:36:21,236
They're waiting.

307
00:36:22,339 --> 00:36:23,599
This way.

308
00:36:58,407 --> 00:37:03,723
My Führer, may I present Colonel Stauffenberg,
our new chief of staff to the reserve army.

309
00:37:04,904 --> 00:37:06,164
Heil, my Führer.

310
00:37:11,559 --> 00:37:18,961
What an honor it is to meet an officer
who has sacrifieced so much for Germany.

311
00:37:24,553 --> 00:37:27,034
And if only more of my men were like you.

312
00:37:29,042 --> 00:37:34,239
Let this man stand as an example to all of you here.
He is the ideal of German officer.

313
00:37:36,208 --> 00:37:37,468
My Führer ...

314
00:37:37,783 --> 00:37:40,973
Colonel Stauffenberg was asked to come
here today to brief us on mobilizing ...

315
00:37:41,209 --> 00:37:45,501
Troops of the reserve army to repell the invasion.

316
00:37:47,312 --> 00:37:48,966
Invasion?

317
00:37:51,210 --> 00:37:52,982
Normandy, my Führer.

318
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:55,739
Oh, yes.

319
00:37:56,959 --> 00:37:58,692
Normandy.

320
00:37:59,755 --> 00:38:01,566
That will not be necessary.

321
00:38:02,708 --> 00:38:07,315
Reichsmarshall Göring assures me
that everything is completely under control.

322
00:38:09,953 --> 00:38:11,292
Thank you, Colonel.

323
00:38:15,427 --> 00:38:21,569
My Führer, if I may. I have an ammended copy
of Operation Valkyrie, for your approval.

324
00:39:10,868 --> 00:39:13,625
You know your Wagner, Colonel?

325
00:39:19,216 --> 00:39:23,351
The Valkyrie, handmaidens of the gods.

326
00:39:23,626 --> 00:39:26,304
Choosing who will live and who will die.

327
00:39:26,540 --> 00:39:32,249
Sparing the most heroic from an agonizing death.

328
00:39:37,329 --> 00:39:40,361
One can not understand National-Socialism

329
00:39:42,094 --> 00:39:44,417
I one does not understand Wagner.

330
00:40:00,010 --> 00:40:03,672
I'm sure whatever changes
you've made are for the best.

331
00:40:08,121 --> 00:40:12,019
You' re dismissed.
Send your man home. And Fromm ...

332
00:40:12,295 --> 00:40:14,815
Have some fresh tea brought in, will you?

333
00:40:25,919 --> 00:40:28,951
I don't know what you're brewing now.
And I don't want to know.

334
00:40:29,581 --> 00:40:34,818
But when the music stops, I'd be obliged
if Keitel found himself without a chair.

335
00:40:47,694 --> 00:40:49,505
Any problem on earth can be solved

336
00:40:49,781 --> 00:40:52,734
With the careful application of high-explosives.

337
00:40:53,246 --> 00:40:55,727
The trick is not te be around when they go off.

338
00:40:56,357 --> 00:41:01,436
Two 975 gram packs of plastic explosives.
Enough explosive to cripple a Panzer.

339
00:41:01,791 --> 00:41:03,484
Your detonators, your fuses.

340
00:41:04,075 --> 00:41:05,768
British time pencils.

341
00:41:06,004 --> 00:41:07,737
This acid capsule is your tirgger.

342
00:41:07,973 --> 00:41:11,989
When you're ready to arm attach the detonator
to the bottom of the time pencil.

343
00:41:12,304 --> 00:41:13,564
Like s.

344
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:17,384
Insert the entire device into
either end of the plastic w*.

345
00:41:17,620 --> 00:41:20,573
Crush the acid capsule.

346
00:41:20,849 --> 00:41:22,739
And you're live.

347
00:41:23,369 --> 00:41:29,905
When the acid eats through the wire holding back
the firing pin, you'll want to be very far away.

348
00:41:33,331 --> 00:41:36,205
For you
- How much time do we have?

349
00:41:36,402 --> 00:41:38,765
Theoretically there's a 30 minute delay,
but with the kind of heat ...

350
00:41:39,001 --> 00:41:42,348
You can expect at the Wolf 's Lair,
I give you 10, 15 minutes, tops.

351
00:41:42,584 --> 00:41:44,199
That's hardly precise.

352
00:41:44,435 --> 00:41:47,940
This is state-of-the-art.
You can have small or precise, not both.

353
00:41:48,176 --> 00:41:50,145
Might this just be a little too small?

354
00:41:51,129 --> 00:41:52,940
Hitler bunker will magnify the blast.

355
00:41:53,177 --> 00:41:56,760
It is constructed of reinforced concrete,
with steel doors, no windows.

356
00:41:56,996 --> 00:42:00,461
The air-pressure generated by just one
of these explosives in a space like that ...

357
00:42:00,697 --> 00:42:04,399
Will kill everyone, instantly.
The second charge will be entirely redundant.

358
00:42:04,596 --> 00:42:07,588
If, by some miracle, Hiltler does survive,
what then?

359
00:42:08,415 --> 00:42:12,943
We sitll initiate Valkyrie.
At that point there'll be no turning back.

360
00:42:13,180 --> 00:42:14,558
But we'll have an advantage.

361
00:42:16,133 --> 00:42:17,983
We have an inside man at the Wolf's Lair.

362
00:42:18,692 --> 00:42:21,409
After the flash he'll cut off
communication with the outside world.

363
00:42:21,606 --> 00:42:23,614
While Hitler's inner-circle
is struggling to regroup ...

364
00:42:23,850 --> 00:42:26,725
We'll have the momentum we need
to seize control in Berlin.

365
00:42:28,497 --> 00:42:31,529
Himmler is expected to be at the meeting as well.
Don't proceed ...

366
00:42:31,804 --> 00:42:33,419
Unless you can get them both.

367
00:42:34,876 --> 00:42:38,577
Don't proceed unless you're confident
you can get both Himmler and Hitler.

368
00:42:45,192 --> 00:42:47,279
This is Goerdeler, isn't it?

369
00:42:51,138 --> 00:42:52,438
Yeah, I'll hold off.

370
00:42:52,674 --> 00:42:55,824
If the decision is unanimous.
But I want another man on the committee.

371
00:42:56,454 --> 00:42:58,895
- Not a politician.
- Who?

372
00:42:59,092 --> 00:43:00,392
Him.

373
00:43:03,817 --> 00:43:05,117
Fine.

374
00:43:05,944 --> 00:43:09,566
But remember, this is a military operation.

375
00:43:09,802 --> 00:43:12,204
Nothing ever goes according to plan.

376
00:43:40,713 --> 00:43:43,469
I'll take the children to Bamberg.

377
00:43:50,163 --> 00:43:51,423
If I fail ...

378
00:43:54,927 --> 00:43:56,266
They'll come for you.

379
00:43:58,432 --> 00:43:59,928
All of you.

380
00:44:03,433 --> 00:44:04,771
I know.

381
00:44:30,484 --> 00:44:32,098
Gentlemen, good morning.

382
00:44:32,374 --> 00:44:35,603
Hitler has scheduled a military briefing
for today, at one o'clock.

383
00:44:36,194 --> 00:44:39,541
- Stauffenberg will start once everyone is present.
- They're here.

384
00:44:39,777 --> 00:44:43,754
Before arming the explosives, Stauffenberg
will call for authorization to proceed.

385
00:44:43,990 --> 00:44:48,124
After the  flash, his inside man
wil sever all communication.

386
00:44:48,755 --> 00:44:52,456
Assuming Fromm refuses to join us,
Olbricht will take command ...

387
00:44:52,692 --> 00:44:55,212
Of the reserve army and initiate Valkyrie.

388
00:44:55,448 --> 00:44:59,622
Then you'll notify all district commanders
that the SS is attempting to seize power.

389
00:44:59,977 --> 00:45:03,836
The reserve army will arrest all SS,
Gestapo and Nazi officials.

390
00:45:04,032 --> 00:45:08,246
By then Stauffenberg will have returned
to Berlin and taken command of the reserve army.

391
00:45:08,797 --> 00:45:11,593
Witzleben and I will assume the role
of commander of the armed forces,

392
00:45:11,829 --> 00:45:13,443
And head of state.

393
00:45:13,680 --> 00:45:18,011
With Berlin secured, Dr. Goerdeler
will address the nation as our new Chancellor.

394
00:45:18,444 --> 00:45:22,264
Then, God willing, we can negotiate
a truce with the allies.

395
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:25,296
Save Europe from total destruction.

396
00:45:27,264 --> 00:45:33,840
This will identify you as a member of the operation,
Nobody goes in or out of the parimeter without one.

397
00:45:34,943 --> 00:45:36,242
Gentlemen.

398
00:45:36,872 --> 00:45:39,471
This is the most important day of your lives.

399
00:45:41,637 --> 00:45:43,842
Long live sacred Germany.

400
00:46:20,619 --> 00:46:22,942
- What is it?
- An order from General Olbricht's office.

401
00:46:23,218 --> 00:46:28,297
He is calling the reserve army for some sort of standby action in all the military districts, including Berlin.

402
00:46:29,242 --> 00:46:32,707
Looks like a drill of some kind.
Send it through, Sergeant.

403
00:46:57,593 --> 00:47:03,106
- Standby action, what the hell for?
- The order doesn't say.

404
00:47:04,208 --> 00:47:05,547
Assemble the men.

405
00:47:06,059 --> 00:47:08,106
This better not be a drill.

406
00:48:44,972 --> 00:48:47,452
The men are assembled
and awaiting further orders.

407
00:48:48,004 --> 00:48:50,721
What do you suppose this is really all about?

408
00:50:39,162 --> 00:50:40,462
You may pass.

409
00:51:07,041 --> 00:51:08,301
Your man?

410
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:20,586
He is now.

411
00:52:37,330 --> 00:52:38,590
Colonel.

412
00:52:50,167 --> 00:52:51,427
Attention.

413
00:53:02,964 --> 00:53:05,956
Gentlemen, for our first order of business ...

414
00:53:06,193 --> 00:53:10,170
General Fromm will present his plans
for the re-allocation of troops ...

415
00:53:10,642 --> 00:53:12,453
From the reserve army on the Eastern front.

416
00:53:12,690 --> 00:53:16,942
But as you know, last night the Russians launched
a new offensive against army group North Ukrain.

417
00:53:17,179 --> 00:53:19,029
In the south Poland sector.

418
00:53:19,266 --> 00:53:24,896
General Harpel was brought in to replace Model
and bring a swift end to this confrontation.

419
00:53:25,133 --> 00:53:28,204
Himmler's not here.
- ... could tranfer three divisions,

420
00:53:28,440 --> 00:53:32,693
To fortify General Harpels troops.

421
00:53:32,929 --> 00:53:37,182
Now these divisions will stick
to a mobile defense plan.

422
00:53:37,457 --> 00:53:40,568
... rather than holding any one particular ...

423
00:53:48,286 --> 00:53:51,003
Connect me to the War Ministry,
General Olbrichts office.

424
00:53:57,027 --> 00:53:59,114
- General Olbrichts office.
- Himmler's not at the briefing,

425
00:53:59,350 --> 00:54:00,847
Awaiting word on permission to proceed.

426
00:54:01,083 --> 00:54:02,343
Hold the line.

427
00:54:02,737 --> 00:54:06,281
Stauffenberg says Himmler's not
at the briefing. He wants to proceed.

428
00:54:06,517 --> 00:54:07,777
Call Beck.

429
00:54:11,360 --> 00:54:13,408
Himmler's not at the briefing.

430
00:54:36,206 --> 00:54:37,939
They say no.

431
00:54:40,735 --> 00:54:42,113
What do you say?

432
00:54:47,074 --> 00:54:48,452
I say do it.

433
00:55:24,166 --> 00:55:28,143
Whatever it was, Colonel,
I hope it was important.

434
00:55:29,915 --> 00:55:32,396
Colonel, your bag.

435
00:55:55,667 --> 00:55:59,290
This has been a drill, you're dismissed.

436
00:56:02,834 --> 00:56:05,944
How dare you put the reserve army
on standby without my knowledge?

437
00:56:06,141 --> 00:56:07,520
Damn near cost me my comission.

438
00:56:07,716 --> 00:56:10,276
And what in God's name made you think
you even had the authority?

439
00:56:10,552 --> 00:56:13,308
It was only a drill, an exercise.
- Don 't lie to me Olbright, not to me.

440
00:56:15,355 --> 00:56:17,639
We both know it wasn't a drill.
- General, if I may ...

441
00:56:17,915 --> 00:56:20,789
No, you may not. Colonel,
you may not do anything.

442
00:56:21,026 --> 00:56:24,845
Because not only have you proved to me you
can't deliver, you've painted a target on my back.

443
00:56:25,829 --> 00:56:29,413
If I so much as sense you're trying
to move the reserve army again ...

444
00:56:29,649 --> 00:56:31,696
I will personally have you both arrested.

445
00:56:34,295 --> 00:56:37,091
Do I make myself abundantly clear?

446
00:56:47,289 --> 00:56:49,416
I'll hear you say it, Colonel.

447
00:57:09,694 --> 00:57:12,884
The point of replacing Hitler is
to negotiate a truce with the allies.

448
00:57:13,159 --> 00:57:15,404
The allies, I suspect,
would be more amenable to a truce ...

449
00:57:15,640 --> 00:57:18,200
If we offered it to them
before they get to fucking Berlin.

450
00:57:18,436 --> 00:57:21,350
There's no point in killing Hitler
unless you kill Himmler too.

451
00:57:21,625 --> 00:57:24,264
Why remove a madman just to have a lunatic
take his place.

452
00:57:24,460 --> 00:57:26,784
Todays failure had nothing to do
with Himmler, and you know it.

453
00:57:27,059 --> 00:57:30,091
This is a military operation in the hands
of a politician, nothing more.

454
00:57:30,367 --> 00:57:32,808
What are you suggesting?
- I'm not suggesting anything.

455
00:57:33,044 --> 00:57:34,738
I'm stating the facts as I see them.

456
00:57:35,013 --> 00:57:37,612
You don't have the courage to kill Hitler,
so you're making the task impossible.

457
00:57:37,888 --> 00:57:39,345
Nothing seems to stop you and your henchmen ...

458
00:57:39,581 --> 00:57:42,810
- From trying it on your own.
- What I regret is that I waited for you to find your backbone.

459
00:57:43,007 --> 00:57:45,920
I don't think I am alone when I say
your judgement is in question.

460
00:57:46,117 --> 00:57:47,810
I'd like to call a vote.

461
00:57:48,047 --> 00:57:52,299
I propose that we relieve Colonel Stauffenberg.

462
00:57:52,929 --> 00:57:57,654
Carl, can I have a word with you in private?
- If you got something to say, say it.

463
00:57:57,891 --> 00:58:01,553
Very well. I heard from the chief
of police this evening ...

464
00:58:01,750 --> 00:58:04,191
that Himmler has issued
a warrant for your arrest.

465
00:58:07,302 --> 00:58:09,231
You have to leave Germany tonight.

466
00:58:09,664 --> 00:58:15,137
When we succeed with the central solution
you'll return as Chancellor.

467
00:58:15,374 --> 00:58:19,666
Disappearing Carl.
Avoid contact with anyone.

468
00:58:33,487 --> 00:58:34,825
Good luck, Colonel.

469
00:58:41,716 --> 00:58:45,890
Nno more indecision.
From now on Stauffenberg has full discretion.

470
00:58:46,126 --> 00:58:48,725
I can't issue the alert again
unless we follow through.

471
00:58:48,962 --> 00:58:52,466
I'll do my job. You just take Berlin.

472
00:58:59,593 --> 00:59:03,058
- Hold on. sir. I have the connection right now.
- Thank you.

473
00:59:12,823 --> 00:59:17,076
I'm sorry, sir. There's bombing in Emmingen.
We've been disconnected.

474
00:59:18,454 --> 00:59:22,510
Emmingen is a long way from Bamberg.
I'm sure your family is safe.

475
01:00:58,194 --> 01:01:01,816
- Welcome, Colonel.
- Do you have a place where I can change, Major?

476
01:01:03,352 --> 01:01:04,809
Please follow me.

477
01:01:11,936 --> 01:01:15,204
- Please, put the reserve army on standby alert.
- Not until I've heard from Stauffenberg.

478
01:01:15,401 --> 01:01:16,976
- Not until I'm sure.
- That's not what he would...

479
01:01:17,212 --> 01:01:19,142
Noted, Colonel.
Thank you.

480
01:01:30,837 --> 01:01:33,278
The meeting has been moved out to 12.30.

481
01:01:33,514 --> 01:01:38,397
Mussolini's arriving on the afternoon train.
The Füher wants to have luncheon.

482
01:01:38,672 --> 01:01:40,641
Will Mussolini be joining us in the briefing, sir?

483
01:01:41,862 --> 01:01:44,539
Only wish he were.
Then some ambitious officer ...

484
01:01:44,776 --> 01:01:47,847
Might take the opportunity
to shoot that deigo bastard.

485
01:01:49,698 --> 01:01:54,423
Excuse me, General. I'm expecting an important call.
Could you please have someone come and get me?

486
01:01:54,659 --> 01:01:56,234
Even if I'm with the Führer.

487
01:01:57,179 --> 01:01:59,817
- Ofcourse, Colonel.
- Thank you sir.

488
01:02:00,172 --> 01:02:02,219
Colonel.

489
01:02:34,114 --> 01:02:35,728
Major Freyend speaking.

490
01:02:45,533 --> 01:02:46,793
Colonel.

491
01:02:47,462 --> 01:02:49,116
They insist you hurry.

492
01:02:49,431 --> 01:02:53,015
- The briefing's about to begin.
- One moment please, Major.

493
01:02:59,669 --> 01:03:04,512
Ten minutes: two for the welcome, one for the
checkpoint, one for the bunker, six to get out.

494
01:03:04,788 --> 01:03:06,284
Plenty of time.

495
01:03:10,261 --> 01:03:11,561
Excuse me, Colonel.

496
01:03:14,356 --> 01:03:16,522
Sir, the Führer's at the briefing.

497
01:03:21,956 --> 01:03:24,122
The Colonel is changing, Major.

498
01:03:27,823 --> 01:03:31,327
- Well, you understand this can be difficult.
- Ofcourse.

499
01:03:45,621 --> 01:03:47,354
Plenty of time.

500
01:04:10,940 --> 01:04:12,200
Get the car.

501
01:04:13,814 --> 01:04:15,980
I've everything I need.
Get the car.

502
01:04:43,701 --> 01:04:45,315
I can manage this.

503
01:04:57,876 --> 01:04:59,727
- Where're they going?
- It is too hot.

504
01:04:59,963 --> 01:05:02,129
The briefing has been moved
to the conference hut.

505
01:05:26,818 --> 01:05:31,306
Major, my injuries have left me hard of hearing.
Would you place me as close to the Führer as possible.

506
01:05:31,503 --> 01:05:33,236
I'll see what I can do.

507
01:05:34,535 --> 01:05:37,390
<i>Not only have they been
advancing from the east,</i>

508
01:05:37,391 --> 01:05:40,245
<i>but they're coming down on the northern
and the southern fronts as well.</i>

509
01:05:42,647 --> 01:05:43,946
<i>As you can see, my Führer ...</i>

510
01:05:44,182 --> 01:05:49,341
<i>If the enemy continues at this rate the situation
in the east Prussian sector is critical.</i>

511
01:05:49,774 --> 01:05:52,569
<i>Lack of supplies is continuing
to weaken our main units.</i>

512
01:05:52,806 --> 01:05:55,286
<i>And reserves are severely depleted.</i>

513
01:05:55,523 --> 01:05:57,807
My Führer, you remember Colonel Stauffenberg?

514
01:06:05,839 --> 01:06:10,958
<i>As you're all aware, in the past 2 days alone,
the 10th Army has given up Ancona.</i>

515
01:06:11,431 --> 01:06:13,754
<i>And the 14th Division has been
pushed out of the...</i>

516
01:06:13,990 --> 01:06:18,046
<i>Army Group Center has already
lost 28 of their 40 divisions.</i>

517
01:06:18,676 --> 01:06:21,983
<i>That is a total of almost 350.000 men.</i>

518
01:06:26,630 --> 01:06:30,331
<i>Since the Red Army first attacked
nearly a month ago.</i>

519
01:06:30,607 --> 01:06:34,033
<i>Our troops have already been
pushed back to the Polish border.</i>

520
01:06:37,222 --> 01:06:39,663
<i>Pondered with the loss of the 4th Army in Minsk.</i>

521
01:06:41,632 --> 01:06:42,892
Yes sir.

522
01:06:43,522 --> 01:06:47,617
<i>From Army Group North Ukraine
as well as the Romanian.</i>

523
01:06:53,012 --> 01:06:55,099
<i>...prevent further losses.</i>

524
01:06:55,099 --> 01:06:57,993
Unless we can quickly dispatch
new blocking divisions,

525
01:06:57,994 --> 01:07:00,887
at vital points along the German right.

526
01:07:01,045 --> 01:07:05,258
<i>Army Group will be swallowed by the
enemies in less than a fortnight.</i>

527
01:07:05,494 --> 01:07:11,400
<i>And we run the risk of losing all the ground
we have managed to gain in the last three years.</i>

528
01:07:13,094 --> 01:07:16,047
General Fellgiebel, sir.
He said it's urgent.

529
01:07:19,118 --> 01:07:21,087
Yes General, this is Stauffenberg.

530
01:07:24,080 --> 01:07:29,238
<i>Russian air activity has proven
just as impregnable as their ground force.</i>

531
01:07:38,216 --> 01:07:40,302
<i>... Some areas they outnumber ...</i>

532
01:07:44,004 --> 01:07:46,051
<i>... along the Italian front, I further ...</i>

533
01:07:48,965 --> 01:07:54,242
<i>One thing is certain, the Red Army will
continue an agressive push west.</i>

534
01:07:54,635 --> 01:07:55,856
Even at the expense ...

535
01:08:00,030 --> 01:08:02,707
In order to rebuild at this...

536
01:08:07,905 --> 01:08:12,000
... already southwest of Lüneburg
and closing on Army Group ...

537
01:08:15,387 --> 01:08:17,710
It will be a catastrophe.

538
01:08:38,815 --> 01:08:40,115
Get in.

539
01:08:41,769 --> 01:08:43,029
Drive.

540
01:08:43,580 --> 01:08:45,549
I've orders from the Führer.

541
01:08:47,439 --> 01:08:48,738
Drive, drive.

542
01:08:52,321 --> 01:08:53,699
Back to work.

543
01:09:23,862 --> 01:09:28,508
Give me the War Ministry,
General Olbricht, it's urgent.

544
01:09:33,430 --> 01:09:42,171
- General Olbrichts office.
- calling from the...lair...General Olbright...Führer.

545
01:09:47,330 --> 01:09:49,259
- Sever all communications.
- Sir?

546
01:09:49,535 --> 01:09:50,834
Just do it.

547
01:09:53,748 --> 01:09:58,355
- Well, what did he say?
- I can't be sure.

548
01:09:59,103 --> 01:10:00,481
Well, get him back on the line.

549
01:10:03,356 --> 01:10:05,128
Sir, the bomb did go off, that much was clear.

550
01:10:05,364 --> 01:10:08,199
Fellgiebel's next step will be
to sever all communications.

551
01:10:18,712 --> 01:10:21,863
- Sorry, Colonel. No-one gets in or out.
- We have an order from the Führer.

552
01:10:22,059 --> 01:10:23,674
We have to get to the airfield
immediately. Open the gate.

553
01:10:23,949 --> 01:10:28,045
- I'm very sorry sir. But my orders are to keep you ...
- I just gave you an order, Sergeant.

554
01:10:30,565 --> 01:10:31,825
Excuse me.

555
01:10:38,873 --> 01:10:41,078
Colonel Stauffenberg for Fieldmarshall Keitel.

556
01:10:47,536 --> 01:10:50,922
Colonel Stauffenberg was explicit.
We initiate Valyrie, regardless ...

557
01:10:51,198 --> 01:10:55,962
- Only Fromm can initiate ...
- Then tell him Hitler's dead or arrest him. But do it now.

558
01:10:56,199 --> 01:10:58,758
You have to give the order to initiate Valkyrie.
This is our only ...

559
01:10:58,994 --> 01:11:02,459
I am not doing anything until I hear from Fellgiebel.
Get him back on the phone now.

560
01:11:02,696 --> 01:11:04,743
Every second we stand here arguing is a second lost.

561
01:11:04,979 --> 01:11:06,279
The risk is too great.

562
01:11:06,554 --> 01:11:09,232
What about Stauffenberg?
What about his risk?

563
01:11:09,468 --> 01:11:12,146
He did his part, and now you are abandonning him.

564
01:11:12,461 --> 01:11:15,138
Fieldmarshall, sir. Stauffenberg here, a Sergeant ...

565
01:11:15,729 --> 01:11:17,580
Kolbe, sir.

566
01:11:18,643 --> 01:11:22,817
Kolbe won't let me past the main gate.
Yes sir, I explained that.

567
01:11:23,053 --> 01:11:25,573
Perhaps you can make him understand, sir.

568
01:11:30,771 --> 01:11:33,291
Everything is fine now,sir.
Thank you.

569
01:11:36,559 --> 01:11:38,016
Open the gate.

570
01:11:46,954 --> 01:11:49,632
- Please put the reserve army on alert.
- When Stauffenberg returns ...

571
01:11:49,868 --> 01:11:54,278
When he gives me confirmation that Hitler
is dead. Then we'll proceed.

572
01:11:59,594 --> 01:12:03,217
- Where are you going?
- The same place as you are ...

573
01:12:03,413 --> 01:12:04,713
Lunch.

574
01:13:41,696 --> 01:13:44,295
Another standby alert.

575
01:13:46,185 --> 01:13:49,138
Send it through and keep me informed.

576
01:14:14,142 --> 01:14:15,520
Sir, another standby order.

577
01:14:18,119 --> 01:14:20,679
In ancient Greece
you would've been killed for this.

578
01:14:21,978 --> 01:14:24,695
Lucky for you we've evolved.

579
01:14:27,648 --> 01:14:29,263
Assemble the men.

580
01:15:16,278 --> 01:15:18,246
Quiet, isn't it?

581
01:15:19,861 --> 01:15:21,711
I'll see where our driver is.

582
01:15:25,058 --> 01:15:28,957
The Colonel and I are at the airfield.
There is no car, there's no-one here.

583
01:15:31,083 --> 01:15:33,052
You mean to tell me the alert's
only just gone out?

584
01:15:34,469 --> 01:15:36,871
This is Stauffenberg,
give me General Olbricht.

585
01:15:44,589 --> 01:15:46,558
What's this?

586
01:15:52,858 --> 01:15:54,945
- Explain this!
- We did something, while you ...

587
01:15:55,181 --> 01:15:59,079
- We do not know that Hitler is not alive.
- This is about Germany, for God's sake, not you.

588
01:16:08,569 --> 01:16:14,357
General Olbricht's office.
Colonel Stauffenberg. For you, sir.

589
01:16:20,815 --> 01:16:24,201
It's been three hours Olbricht.
What the hell have you been doing?

590
01:16:24,438 --> 01:16:27,351
We've had no confirmation
that Hitler was dead.

591
01:16:28,730 --> 01:16:30,895
Damned, I saw the explosion myself.

592
01:16:31,250 --> 01:16:33,809
- We are committed.
- Dear god.

593
01:16:34,045 --> 01:16:36,054
Now where is Fromm?
Is he with us?

594
01:16:37,629 --> 01:16:39,794
No-one has spoken to him yet.

595
01:16:50,977 --> 01:16:54,915
Listen to me. Never mind Germany,
never mind Europe.

596
01:16:55,190 --> 01:16:59,876
Your life is at stake now. And if you want to live
through the night, you'll do exactly as I say.

597
01:17:00,073 --> 01:17:02,790
The second you hang up the phone
initiate Valkyrie in Fromm's name.

598
01:17:03,026 --> 01:17:06,609
Give him the choice to join us or place him
under immediate arrest, you understand?

599
01:17:07,436 --> 01:17:10,389
I'll be at Fromm's office in 50 minutes.
Be there when I arrive.

600
01:17:40,630 --> 01:17:44,214
Call Beck and others.
Tell them it's time.

601
01:17:49,293 --> 01:17:51,459
Put me through to communications.

602
01:17:52,758 --> 01:17:56,420
This is General Olbricht.
Calling on behalf of General Fromm ...

603
01:17:56,656 --> 01:18:00,712
Commander of the reserve army.
The Führer, Adolf Hitler, is dead.

604
01:18:00,948 --> 01:18:04,256
A group of radicals in the SS are attempting
to seize control of the government.

605
01:18:04,492 --> 01:18:07,760
Initiate operation Valkyrie.

606
01:18:41,624 --> 01:18:44,892
You have your orders. Pass them along.

607
01:19:20,764 --> 01:19:22,339
Battalion.

608
01:19:22,772 --> 01:19:24,111
Attention.

609
01:19:32,262 --> 01:19:35,963
Our Führer, Adolf Hitler ...

610
01:19:38,010 --> 01:19:40,176
Is dead.

611
01:19:40,412 --> 01:19:42,027
Who told you the Führer was dead?

612
01:19:42,302 --> 01:19:44,862
General Fellgiebel, at the Wolf's Lair.

613
01:19:47,421 --> 01:19:50,138
There's no use calling.
All communication lines are down.

614
01:19:50,335 --> 01:19:51,713
Get me the Wolf's Lair.

615
01:19:57,856 --> 01:20:01,045
Yes, General Fromm for
Fieldmarshall Keitel, urgent.

616
01:20:05,731 --> 01:20:09,984
I am sorry to disturb you, sir. But I wonder
if you could tell me what's happening?

617
01:20:10,220 --> 01:20:13,921
- The most incredible rumours are circulating in Berlin.
- I don't know what you mean.

618
01:20:14,158 --> 01:20:17,465
There's talk that the Führer has been assassinated.

619
01:20:19,080 --> 01:20:23,608
Another failed attempt.
The Führer was never in danger.

620
01:20:24,041 --> 01:20:27,782
By the way, where is your man, Stauffenberg?

621
01:20:28,018 --> 01:20:31,365
Stauffenberg? On his way back to Berlin,
I would think.

622
01:20:32,153 --> 01:20:35,657
Let me know when he arrives.
I'd like a word with him.

623
01:20:42,508 --> 01:20:44,753
- The Führer's fine.
- That is a lie.

624
01:20:44,950 --> 01:20:47,155
Adolf Hitler is dead.
Operation Valkyrie is in effect.

625
01:20:47,391 --> 01:20:50,502
- Only I can initiate Valkyrie.
- You did.

626
01:20:59,322 --> 01:21:00,621
This is treason.

627
01:21:00,858 --> 01:21:03,142
Right now, the reserve army
is assuming control of Berlin.

628
01:21:03,378 --> 01:21:06,843
- Are you with us or not?
- Do you realise what you've done?

629
01:21:07,040 --> 01:21:08,497
The Führer is alive.

630
01:21:08,733 --> 01:21:12,631
I delivered the bomb myself,
I saw the blast. He is dead.

631
01:21:14,561 --> 01:21:17,120
- Are you with us?
- I don't believe this is happening. This is some kind of..

632
01:21:17,356 --> 01:21:19,286
Are you with us or not?

633
01:21:19,640 --> 01:21:25,271
Colonel, if what you say is true
you should shoot yourself immediately.

634
01:21:25,507 --> 01:21:28,382
- The rest of you are under arrest.
- No General, you are.

635
01:21:34,091 --> 01:21:36,808
I don't know where you think this is going.

636
01:21:39,643 --> 01:21:40,943
Get me operations.

637
01:21:42,557 --> 01:21:46,298
This is Colonel Stauffenberg, seal off
the War Ministery per operation Valkyrie.

638
01:21:46,534 --> 01:21:50,393
No-one gets in or out without authorization
from General Olbricht's office.

639
01:22:06,576 --> 01:22:07,876
General Beck.

640
01:22:09,490 --> 01:22:10,947
You're not wearing your uniform, sir.

641
01:22:11,223 --> 01:22:13,546
This should be seen as a movement of the people.

642
01:22:19,531 --> 01:22:20,870
Colonel Stauffenberg.

643
01:22:27,131 --> 01:22:30,320
The chief has guaranteed the full support
of the Berlin police.

644
01:22:32,880 --> 01:22:36,817
You will have no interference from my men.
You have my word.

645
01:22:39,692 --> 01:22:41,031
Thank you.

646
01:23:15,406 --> 01:23:18,674
Colonel Stauffenberg, sir.
We're reporting for duty.

647
01:23:24,069 --> 01:23:25,801
Thank you for coming.

648
01:23:29,975 --> 01:23:33,834
Gentlemen.
In three hours I wantconfirmation ...

649
01:23:34,070 --> 01:23:38,559
That we in government quarter's ours and
SS command has been cleared of every living soul.

650
01:23:39,701 --> 01:23:41,237
You all know what must be done.

651
01:23:42,654 --> 01:23:46,946
By nightfall I want to know that Hitler's
Germany has seen its last sunrise.

652
01:24:17,502 --> 01:24:22,975
Feldmarschall Witzleben has been appointed
commander in chief of the armed forces.

653
01:24:23,211 --> 01:24:27,188
That's exactly why he's been appointed. If he was
a member of the Party he'd be locked up as a suspect.

654
01:24:27,425 --> 01:24:31,205
- Yes sir, I understand. This is an emergency.
- Commanding officer of the 11th district ...

655
01:24:31,402 --> 01:24:35,261
- I need a decision, Major.
- Tell your men that acts of vengeance will not be tolerated.

656
01:24:35,497 --> 01:24:39,119
- Connect me to the commanding officer in Hannover ...
- We represent a different form of  government.

657
01:24:39,316 --> 01:24:42,073
I'd be careful who you said that to.
Loyalty to the Party isn't what it used to be.

658
01:24:42,309 --> 01:24:43,805
Yes, Paris, France.

659
01:24:44,002 --> 01:24:45,813
Heads of state murdered the Führer.

660
01:24:46,050 --> 01:24:47,861
Thank you, you made the right decision.

661
01:24:49,830 --> 01:24:51,168
District 13 is ours.

662
01:25:02,706 --> 01:25:06,683
You're under arrest for crimes against the state.

663
01:25:15,936 --> 01:25:18,023
This is Stauffenberg, I'm trying to connect
with Major-General Todt.

664
01:25:18,220 --> 01:25:21,134
... 413 battalion, you have no trouble getting ...

665
01:25:21,370 --> 01:25:23,772
... This is Colonel Stauffenberg
.... will explain everything ...

666
01:25:24,520 --> 01:25:25,819
... Excellent.

667
01:25:27,631 --> 01:25:32,198
My wife is at Bamberg with my children,
would you please try to reach them with the phone?

668
01:25:32,395 --> 01:25:33,695
Thank you.

669
01:25:33,892 --> 01:25:36,805
General Scheidler has issued the Valkyrie
orders and has sealed off headquarters.

670
01:25:37,002 --> 01:25:40,231
Check on the radio stations every 20 minutes
until we have confirmation they're ours.

671
01:25:52,831 --> 01:25:55,115
With all due respect, sir.
You can't believe everything you hear.

672
01:25:55,391 --> 01:25:59,604
That is SS propaganda, he's dead. The commander
of the home army is authorized to give orders.

673
01:26:01,140 --> 01:26:02,400
General.

674
01:26:04,959 --> 01:26:07,637
Our men in the transport office have secured
the railways communications network.

675
01:26:07,873 --> 01:26:09,803
... repeat to stations ...

676
01:26:15,079 --> 01:26:16,772
He's with us.

677
01:26:17,323 --> 01:26:20,749
Mertz, call Potsdam, tell them place
all available units under our control.

678
01:26:21,025 --> 01:26:22,679
You have your men, now get control ...

679
01:26:22,915 --> 01:26:24,569
We have control of the government quarter.

680
01:26:24,805 --> 01:26:26,262
We don't have Berlin yet.

681
01:26:48,903 --> 01:26:51,502
- What is it now, Sergeant?
- Arrest orders, sir.

682
01:26:51,777 --> 01:26:53,589
One from Colonel Stauffenberg
in the War Ministry.

683
01:26:53,864 --> 01:26:55,282
To arrest Reichsminister Goebbels.

684
01:26:55,991 --> 01:27:00,165
The other is from the Wolfs Lair
to arrest Colonel Stauffenberg.

685
01:27:05,441 --> 01:27:06,977
Send them both through.

686
01:27:08,119 --> 01:27:10,442
Our job is not to interpret orders.

687
01:27:10,643 --> 01:27:12,765
Our job is to pass them
along, regardless ...

688
01:27:13,434 --> 01:27:15,994
- Yes, but...
- That will be all, Sergeant.

689
01:27:51,629 --> 01:27:54,740
New arrest orders, sir.
For Stauffenberg and Goebbels.

690
01:27:56,827 --> 01:27:58,914
Do we arrest them both?

691
01:27:59,780 --> 01:28:02,143
I would hate to find out
I am being taken advantage of.

692
01:28:02,339 --> 01:28:03,914
You really think it's a coup?

693
01:28:04,387 --> 01:28:05,686
I'm afraid so.

694
01:28:06,080 --> 01:28:08,403
But I can't say which side we're on.

695
01:28:09,624 --> 01:28:10,884
Come with me.

696
01:28:21,437 --> 01:28:23,209
I've just spoken to Colonel...

697
01:28:23,248 --> 01:28:26,910
They've arrested 1200 SS
and Gestapo officials in Paris.

698
01:28:27,186 --> 01:28:28,840
Not a single shot fired.

699
01:28:29,076 --> 01:28:32,501
Early reports from Vienna are good.
I'm waiting on word from Prague.

700
01:29:06,404 --> 01:29:08,176
I am ready to be connected.

701
01:29:21,840 --> 01:29:23,139
Minister Goebbels?

702
01:29:23,809 --> 01:29:25,265
What can I do for you, Major?

703
01:29:25,699 --> 01:29:28,572
My battalion has an order
to block every government quarter,

704
01:29:28,599 --> 01:29:31,172
and place you under arrest.

705
01:29:34,046 --> 01:29:36,645
Are you a dedicated National-Socialist, Major?

706
01:29:38,246 --> 01:29:39,246
Yes, Sir.

707
01:29:53,065 --> 01:29:54,404
Major Remer here.

708
01:29:59,759 --> 01:30:02,358
Do you recognize my voice?

709
01:30:04,051 --> 01:30:07,083
- Yes, my Führer.
- Then listen to me very carefully.

710
01:30:09,800 --> 01:30:16,297
- I want these traitors taken alive.
- Yes, my Führer.

711
01:30:20,392 --> 01:30:24,763
You heard what he said.
The Führer wants the traitors taken alive.

712
01:30:26,220 --> 01:30:27,480
Yes sir.

713
01:30:52,090 --> 01:30:53,429
It is a coup alright.

714
01:30:54,334 --> 01:30:56,854
We can't afford
to remain neutral any longer.

715
01:31:00,122 --> 01:31:02,721
You have to make a decision.

716
01:31:04,493 --> 01:31:07,328
When it's over we better land
on the right side.

717
01:31:17,881 --> 01:31:19,653
Send through all communication
from the Wolf's Lair

718
01:31:19,889 --> 01:31:21,819
Stop all communications
from Stauffenberg.

719
01:31:28,355 --> 01:31:29,891
Release these men.

720
01:31:31,505 --> 01:31:33,080
Sir, they're part of the coup.

721
01:31:33,395 --> 01:31:38,632
I've just been on the phone
with Hitler himself. We've been duped.

722
01:31:42,137 --> 01:31:44,184
We've lost contact with district 11.

723
01:31:47,649 --> 01:31:50,878
The switchboard is overloaded.
Give it ten minutes, then try again.

724
01:31:55,525 --> 01:31:58,005
Give me General Vieler, district 11.

725
01:31:58,202 --> 01:32:01,864
- We still need our ...
- Keep trying.

726
01:32:04,069 --> 01:32:05,566
Where is General Fromm?

727
01:32:08,007 --> 01:32:10,488
General Fromm is no longer in command,
I am.

728
01:32:12,693 --> 01:32:15,331
- Beck, what are you doing here? What is going on?
- The Führer is dead.

729
01:32:15,567 --> 01:32:18,560
The SS are staging a coup, we've
initiated operation Valkyrie ...

730
01:32:18,796 --> 01:32:21,119
To crush the uprising
and save Hitler's Germany.

731
01:32:21,355 --> 01:32:23,442
You'll present the order to your troops.

732
01:32:24,584 --> 01:32:27,577
I will do no such thing
until I speak to General Fromm.

733
01:32:27,774 --> 01:32:30,806
You'll follow your orders
or you are arrested.

734
01:32:32,026 --> 01:32:33,759
This is treason.

735
01:32:34,704 --> 01:32:38,011
I will take no part.
The Führer is not dead.

736
01:32:38,604 --> 01:32:42,811
The Führer is not dead!
- Stop him!  - The Führer is not dead...

737
01:32:44,304 --> 01:32:48,911
I sworn an oath! This is treason!
You all sworn an oath!

738
01:32:49,115 --> 01:32:53,880
Listen to what I have to say!
You are all making a terrible mistake!

739
01:32:54,416 --> 01:33:00,954
The Führer is not dead!
The Führer is not dead!

740
01:33:02,740 --> 01:33:04,275
Please try my wife again...

741
01:32:54,116 --> 01:32:56,754
The Führer is not dead.

742
01:33:02,740 --> 01:33:04,275
Please try my wife again.

743
01:33:13,040 --> 01:33:14,275
Bamberg, please...

744
01:33:21,240 --> 01:33:22,675
Get your hands off!

745
01:33:28,640 --> 01:33:29,475
Sir...

746
01:33:39,940 --> 01:33:44,475
<i>"... Over 215 enemy tanks have been annahilated
in the past week alone."</i>

747
01:33:44,900 --> 01:33:48,475
<i>"The Airforce engaged a low-flying offensive
on enemy concentrations..."</i>

748
01:33:49,873 --> 01:33:51,023
I can't get through to General Goerlock.

749
01:33:51,100 --> 01:33:53,023
Send a runner down to his office,
bring him here.

750
01:33:56,700 --> 01:33:57,823
Yes, thank you.

751
01:33:59,166 --> 01:34:01,334
Yes, this is Stauffenberg.

752
01:34:01,335 --> 01:34:03,502
I was speaking to the
General 5 minutes ago.

753
01:34:03,566 --> 01:34:05,702
He told me he'll return my call...

754
01:34:05,938 --> 01:34:08,655
I trust everything in your district
is under control.

755
01:34:12,238 --> 01:34:14,209
And the General knows I'm waiting?

756
01:34:15,238 --> 01:34:16,385
I'm ordering you to put him
on the phone immediately.

757
01:34:16,385 --> 01:34:18,775
<i>... the army gave their oath to a liar, Hans...
- Hello?</i>

758
01:34:19,485 --> 01:34:21,230
<i>... One who has broken his own oath
to the people a hundred times over...</i>

759
01:34:21,231 --> 01:34:22,975
- Hello?

760
01:34:23,461 --> 01:34:24,839
Hans, listen to me.

761
01:34:50,709 --> 01:34:53,859
This operation has been terminated!
Stand down!

762
01:34:58,781 --> 01:35:01,419
<i>"Today an attempt was made on the Führer's life."</i>

763
01:35:01,774 --> 01:35:06,381
<i>"The Führer himself suffered no major injuries
beyond light burns and bruises"</i>

764
01:35:06,617 --> 01:35:08,669
<i>"He resumed his work immediately."</i>

765
01:35:08,700 --> 01:35:14,369
<i>"No seriously wounded include General...,
Colonel Brandt and staff-officer Berger..."</i>

766
01:35:19,493 --> 01:35:22,800
Send the following orders to all
reserve army commanders:

767
01:35:22,893 --> 01:35:25,911
"Broadcast incorrect. The Führer is dead..."

768
01:35:28,313 --> 01:35:30,400
"Operation Valkyrie still in effect."

769
01:35:30,620 --> 01:35:35,600
<i>"... Reich Marshal Goering, and has scheduled
to receive Mussolini..."</i>

770
01:35:35,813 --> 01:35:41,800
<i>"... Long live our Fuhrer, Adolf Hitler, whom
the Almighty God has so visibly blessed today."</i>

771
01:35:45,127 --> 01:35:46,505
I saw the blast.

772
01:35:51,545 --> 01:35:53,317
I saw the blast.

773
01:36:01,980 --> 01:36:04,775
<i>"Today an attempt was made on the Führer's life."</i>

774
01:36:05,051 --> 01:36:08,122
<i>"The Führer himself suffered no major injuries
beyond light burns and bruises ..."</i>

775
01:36:09,551 --> 01:36:10,286
I'm sorry...

776
01:36:10,287 --> 01:36:14,022
<i>"... resumed his work immediately.
No seriously wounded..."</i>

777
01:36:39,351 --> 01:36:42,522
<i>"Stay tuned for the Fuhrer's address
to the German people."</i>

778
01:36:42,025 --> 01:36:46,986
- My family?
- Our lines have been cut.

779
01:36:50,215 --> 01:36:51,554
I'm sorry.

780
01:36:53,129 --> 01:36:54,429
Go.

781
01:36:55,925 --> 01:36:58,012
It's alright. Go.

782
01:37:13,723 --> 01:37:16,755
General, sir.
We have to get you out of here.

783
01:38:39,923 --> 01:38:41,155
Get back.

784
01:38:41,610 --> 01:38:43,422
- Stop.
- Stand down.

785
01:38:43,658 --> 01:38:45,784
- I said stop.
- I said stand down.

786
01:39:11,890 --> 01:39:13,623
Hold your fire.

787
01:39:22,364 --> 01:39:24,333
Colonel Stauffenberg.

788
01:39:26,932 --> 01:39:29,885
By orders of the Führer,
you are under arrest.

789
01:39:51,700 --> 01:39:55,421
If you have any last messages
to your wives and children,

790
01:39:55,522 --> 01:39:56,543
I will hear them now.

791
01:39:58,472 --> 01:40:01,662
Very well, a court martial convened by me ...

792
01:40:01,937 --> 01:40:03,591
in the Führer's absence,
will pronounce sentence.

793
01:40:03,828 --> 01:40:05,324
Beck, you are under arrest.

794
01:40:05,599 --> 01:40:10,561
Colonel Mertz von Quirnheim,
General Olbricht, Lieutenant Haeften,

795
01:40:10,836 --> 01:40:14,223
And the Colonel, whose name I will
not mention, are condemned to death.

796
01:40:14,459 --> 01:40:16,703
General, my orders are
to take these men alive.

797
01:40:16,940 --> 01:40:18,200
Noted, Major.

798
01:40:19,932 --> 01:40:22,137
I'd like a pistol, please.

799
01:40:24,461 --> 01:40:26,626
For personal reasons.

800
01:40:43,676 --> 01:40:45,881
- Get on with it.
- With all respect, sir.

801
01:40:46,117 --> 01:40:47,417
That will be all, Major.

802
01:40:47,692 --> 01:40:49,583
Killing us won't hide your involvement.

803
01:40:49,858 --> 01:40:52,181
My involvement?
I don't know what you're talking about?

804
01:40:52,575 --> 01:40:55,607
- You knew and did nothing.
- You're as guilty as any of us.

805
01:40:55,843 --> 01:40:59,978
- Spare me Lieutenant.
- No one will be spared.

806
01:41:14,586 --> 01:41:17,106
I'm thinking of earlier times.

807
01:41:21,871 --> 01:41:25,966
This is an outrage.
It has never before been perpetrated here.

808
01:41:26,202 --> 01:41:29,589
A Field Marshal and a General declare
that they could do things better than he...

809
01:41:29,589 --> 01:41:33,251
Who is the Füher of us all.

810
01:41:33,526 --> 01:41:36,164
You'll protest to having said this?

811
01:41:42,031 --> 01:41:46,717
<i>My fellow Germans.
I speak to you tonight for two reasons.</i>

812
01:41:46,953 --> 01:41:51,482
<i>First, so that you can hear my voice
and know that I am unhurt.</i>

813
01:41:51,915 --> 01:41:56,089
<i>Second, so that you can know
the details of a crime ...</i>

814
01:41:56,325 --> 01:41:58,648
<i>without parallel in German history.</i>

815
01:41:59,396 --> 01:42:05,815
<i>A small clique of ambitious, dishonorable
officers had conspired to eliminate me.</i>

816
01:42:07,193 --> 01:42:09,595
<i>Except for a few bruises and burns ...</i>

817
01:42:09,870 --> 01:42:12,548
<i>I was completely untouched.</i>

818
01:42:14,005 --> 01:42:16,840
<i>I see in this the hand of Providence ...</i>

819
01:42:17,864 --> 01:42:20,817
<i>Directing me to complete my work.</i>

820
01:42:29,480 --> 01:42:31,252
Look them in the eye.

821
01:42:33,220 --> 01:42:34,914
They'll remember you.

822
01:42:35,620 --> 01:42:37,414
Olbricht!

823
01:42:47,020 --> 01:42:48,614
Men, ready!

824
01:43:03,289 --> 01:43:07,478
And we have to show the world,
that not all of us were like him.

825
01:43:12,289 --> 01:43:14,478
Safe!
Stand!

826
01:43:17,400 --> 01:43:18,200
Agh..

827
01:43:18,200 --> 01:43:21,400
Fire!
Stand!

828
01:43:42,400 --> 01:43:44,100
Stauffenberg!

829
01:43:47,090 --> 01:43:50,949
People know we put our principles
above personal gains.

830
01:43:51,000 --> 01:43:52,659
Men, Ready!

831
01:43:55,920 --> 01:43:56,919
Aim!

832
01:44:12,133 --> 01:44:14,259
Safe. Stand.

833
01:44:20,638 --> 01:44:25,127
You may hand us over to the executioner,
but in three months time...

834
01:44:25,363 --> 01:44:28,947
The disgusted and tired people
will bring you to book.

835
01:44:29,144 --> 01:44:34,111
And drag you alive through
the dirt in the streets.

836
01:44:34,144 --> 01:44:35,211
Take him away!

837
01:44:39,933 --> 01:44:42,413
Men, Ready!

838
01:44:44,697 --> 01:44:45,957
Aim!

839
01:44:47,690 --> 01:44:48,989
- Long live sacred Germany!
- Fire.

840
01:44:51,190 --> 01:44:52,989
Stand.

841
01:46:20,000 --> 01:46:24,000
